WEBVTT

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:07.370
What?!

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.940
The terrorists who destroyed the
boomer just appeared on the roof!

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:15.180
The AD Police are surrounding them!

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:18.580
This had to happen the one day we're off duty.

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:22.810
Our bitter enemy, the Knight Sabers,
are finished now, I guess.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:29.890
They tricked us.

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:32.460
Priss, be careful!

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:36.860
You're being telecast to the whole world now.

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:39.660
Sylia! Linna... Linna fell in!

00:00:57.020 --> 00:00:58.690
Linna, are you okay?

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:00.320
My meter is almost expired.

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:02.480
I'll do something. Stay there!

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:10.260
I found it!

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:11.730
I'm gonna get it!

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:16.390
This suit is so heavy!

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:20.670
Have we been taken for fools by
something as stupid as this?

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:23.840
This is just a threat, Koyama! Don't kill it!

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:26.710
I can't see well, Leader.

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:36.790
Priss, that's not a boomer!

00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:38.780
They're the same. Jerk!

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:41.360
Thank you...

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:42.950
Let's hurry home, okay?

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:01.480
You bastards!

00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:03.380
Damn! It's impossible to not kill them!

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:04.850
Fire!

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:19.200
Nene, Linna!

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:29.110
Priss!

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:32.200
Damn, I can't lose like this!

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:37.680
Damn!

00:02:39.190 --> 00:02:42.020
They're not boomers! Are you
going to kill them?!

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:45.160
You're off today, aren't you?
Mind your own business!

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:46.730
What the hell did you say?!

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:48.230
Cut it out!

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:50.630
I've heard the General Manager approved this.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:56.000
Priss!

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.340
It's over for me. My meter's expired.

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:03.100
This is the end.

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:15.420
Sylia!

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:16.560
What's that?!

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:19.960
I haven't seen that type of
Knight Saber in a long time.

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:30.670
Open fire!

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:35.280
Leon, this isn't good at all!

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:36.540
What's the matter?

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:39.050
What's that?

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:43.720
Call the suppression team!

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:09.900
The boomer destroying terrorists
have escaped from the factory.

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:16.180
Sorry, but our live coverage is now over.

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:21.120
This program was sponsored by Genom
Corporation, leaders in boomer technology.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:30.030
We'll be arriving at the Haneda
Aerospace Port in a short while.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:43.500
Is that fast?

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:49.410
When it's completed, can I try it out?

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:52.020
I'll think about it.

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:55.590
A repair?

00:04:55.590 --> 00:04:56.580
Yes.

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:01.220
No, not that one.

00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:04.590
I got it. I'll go there later.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:07.770
Nigel...

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:12.000
How long have you known Sylia?

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:15.910
For a long time.

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:16.970
I see.

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:38.400
I hate work like this.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:40.870
Ms. Yamazaki!

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:42.570
This is no good.

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:44.910
If one person is in a bad mood,
as you seem to be,

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:47.810
it contaminates the whole
atmosphere of this department.

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:54.780
Manipulating the data is similar to
a human relationship.

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:57.820
If you're not sincere or if you
don't deal with it gently,

00:05:57.820 --> 00:06:01.560
it sometimes gets upset and angry.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:05.390
It might be boring or troublesome
for you to deal with the numbers,

00:06:05.390 --> 00:06:07.490
but work is work, right?

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:12.990
Of course, the only thing you want
to look at is a man, right?

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:17.700
Well, please finish that up today anyway.

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:20.710
Ms. Yamazaki...

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:21.240
Yes?
Ms. Yamazaki...

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:22.210
Yes?
It's good for you to exercise,
but don't overdo it.

00:06:22.210 --> 00:06:25.250
It's good for you to exercise,
but don't overdo it.

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:28.270
Your calves are, well, too muscular.

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:33.110
I'm going to kill him some day!

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:57.770
It's so sad to become unable to
wear the clothes you really like.

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:08.160
Lady Sylia, you have a guest.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:11.960
It must be Nigel. I've been waiting for him.

00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:13.760
No, it's not him.

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:23.690
You!

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:28.310
He insists he's your brother, Lady Sylia.

00:07:28.310 --> 00:07:32.750
I keep telling him that you have no brothers.

00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:33.970
Mackey?

00:07:35.150 --> 00:07:37.180
Sylia...

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:38.920
Why?

00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:41.490
Well, I'm glad you came all the way here.

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:42.990
Lady Sylia!

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:48.020
Oh, no! You shouldn't assume that
I don't have any brothers.

00:07:51.230 --> 00:07:54.000
This boy is surely

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.140
my younger brother.

00:07:56.140 --> 00:07:58.370
Well, come with me, Mackey!

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:00.360
I have to prepare your room, don't I?

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:08.380
Hey, guess what!

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:11.820
I wore my hard suit for the first time in a while!

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:13.890
You shouldn't push yourself too hard.

00:08:13.890 --> 00:08:15.990
You care about me, don't you?

00:08:15.990 --> 00:08:19.160
A person who's able to control the
core unit of the hard suit is...

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:21.430
You don't need to tell me, I know.

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:23.400
I've grown, matured too much for the suit.

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:27.270
How long will it take to fix them?

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:30.300
All three suits, probably a week.

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:31.910
That's too long!

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:34.900
What are you going to do if a
boomer goes mad before then?

00:08:38.180 --> 00:08:40.110
I'm sorry.

00:08:40.110 --> 00:08:41.840
I guess I'm too tired.

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:45.250
Oh yes, my brother just arrived.

00:08:46.550 --> 00:08:50.390
Didn't I tell you I have one?

00:08:50.390 --> 00:08:51.450
A younger brother.

00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:01.570
This is your room.

00:09:01.570 --> 00:09:03.700
Please make yourself at home.

00:09:05.070 --> 00:09:06.110
Excuse me...

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:08.010
Yes, Mr. Mackey?

00:09:08.010 --> 00:09:10.710
Is Sylia still...

00:09:10.710 --> 00:09:12.280
Yes?

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:16.020
Oh, never mind. Sorry.

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:17.280
Mr. Mackey...

00:09:19.850 --> 00:09:24.790
Welcome to Tokyo. We all welcome you.

00:09:38.770 --> 00:09:40.030
Sylia...

00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:59.290
For failing to capture the Knight Sabers,

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:01.780
I will make the General Manager
of the AD Police responsibile.

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:07.830
I've positioned someone there
who will listen without question.

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:15.310
We can't move forward if we repeat
the errors of the past, Mason.

00:10:15.310 --> 00:10:17.140
Yes, Sir.

00:10:17.140 --> 00:10:20.880
Are there any delays in the Showhamm Project?

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:25.950
There's a report of four boomers
doing space work that went mad.

00:10:25.950 --> 00:10:28.660
We disposed of them before they
got really out of control.

00:10:28.660 --> 00:10:32.590
Boomers are growing ever
more like human beings.

00:10:32.590 --> 00:10:34.960
If humans had to keep working in
space for extended periods,

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:39.330
some of them would have gone crazy.

00:10:39.330 --> 00:10:44.470
The frequency of mad boomers
seems to be increasing slowly.

00:10:44.470 --> 00:10:50.210
Boomers should disappear. That's
what you're thinking, aren't you?

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:51.410
No, Sir.

00:10:51.410 --> 00:10:54.550
Let Yoshikiri handle all boomer business.

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:58.310
You need to concentrate on
the Showhamm Project.

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:03.310
Withdraw from the boomers?

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:14.000
Laugh.

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:15.060
Sir?

00:11:16.100 --> 00:11:17.070
Laugh.

00:11:24.310 --> 00:11:28.110
It's me. You haven't found what
we've been looking for, have you?

00:11:28.110 --> 00:11:32.990
The earthquake dispersed the
central stratum everywhere.

00:11:32.990 --> 00:11:35.760
I'm sure it had the power to do that.

00:11:35.760 --> 00:11:39.190
It seems that there's a limit to
searching for it from the surface.

00:11:39.190 --> 00:11:42.220
I understand. I'll think of some
way to deal with it.

00:11:57.810 --> 00:11:58.970
Is something funny?

00:12:00.050 --> 00:12:01.980
No.

00:12:01.980 --> 00:12:04.640
Then don't laugh, my poor doll.

00:12:18.530 --> 00:12:21.030
See? I think this looks really good on you!

00:12:21.030 --> 00:12:22.770
Really?

00:12:22.770 --> 00:12:24.770
Your figure is so beautiful,

00:12:24.770 --> 00:12:26.370
it'd be a waste if you didn't
wear clothes like this!

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:28.170
Is that really true?

00:12:40.120 --> 00:12:41.590
What?

00:13:23.100 --> 00:13:25.790
You look as if you're talking with that machine!

00:13:27.900 --> 00:13:34.470
Machines know when they're
assembled and powered properly.

00:13:36.740 --> 00:13:38.610
You're amazing, Mister!

00:13:38.610 --> 00:13:42.050
I didn't say that you could come in here, did I?

00:13:51.690 --> 00:13:55.130
Well, our meal is ready upstairs.

00:13:55.130 --> 00:13:56.360
Let's eat together.

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:19.550
I'm really happy that you came here.

00:14:21.620 --> 00:14:24.290
I didn't forget about you.

00:14:24.290 --> 00:14:27.850
But I have something to do in this town, so...

00:14:29.360 --> 00:14:33.200
I wish that man downstairs would
come up here and eat with us.

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:36.570
Nigel doesn't like to do things like that.

00:14:36.570 --> 00:14:38.000
That man is incredible, isn't he?

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:40.240
I understand, because I love machines.

00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:42.710
The machine can't use all its power

00:14:42.710 --> 00:14:44.730
if the person who maintains it doesn't love it.

00:14:46.980 --> 00:14:49.950
Don't talk about machines as
if they were human beings!

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:56.290
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to get upset.

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:59.750
It just sometimes happens to me.
Sometimes I can't control myself.

00:15:00.890 --> 00:15:02.900
Oh, no!

00:15:02.900 --> 00:15:05.160
I show that I have my mother's
genes when I get like this.

00:15:13.740 --> 00:15:17.980
That type of character hasn't been
inherited by you, has it?

00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:20.710
Of course not, because I'm a...

00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:29.890
You're my real younger brother, Mackey.

00:15:29.890 --> 00:15:34.350
So you're going to live with me.

00:15:39.270 --> 00:15:43.400
Please hold me tight just once

00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:50.280
After you do, I won't need any
more words from you

00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:54.410
Pretending sadness, I want
to drown myself in love

00:15:54.410 --> 00:16:02.750
It seems so unfriendly,
but it fascinates me

00:16:51.470 --> 00:16:54.510
Hello, Romanova residence!

00:16:54.510 --> 00:16:55.780
It's me.

00:16:55.780 --> 00:16:59.350
Linna, why are you calling in
the middle of the night?

00:16:59.350 --> 00:17:01.780
Right, I'm sorry.

00:17:01.780 --> 00:17:04.220
Did something happen?

00:17:04.220 --> 00:17:06.550
No, not like that.

00:17:11.060 --> 00:17:15.060
Nene, you haven't done any
special training, have you?

00:17:15.060 --> 00:17:16.700
Well...

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:19.770
You see, I'm not good at doing things like that.

00:17:19.770 --> 00:17:23.400
But you're able to move in your
hard suit, aren't you?

00:17:23.400 --> 00:17:25.470
Well, I guess that's my talent, isn't it?

00:17:25.470 --> 00:17:28.410
I'm beautiful, and on top of that,

00:17:28.410 --> 00:17:31.580
I've been blessed with intelligence
and athletic ability,

00:17:31.580 --> 00:17:33.740
so I don't know what to do about it.

00:17:37.880 --> 00:17:40.350
That's just a joke.

00:17:40.350 --> 00:17:42.820
I knew that.

00:17:42.820 --> 00:17:45.690
Take less time to show it.

00:17:45.690 --> 00:17:49.130
I've been going to the gym every day,

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:51.460
but I feel like I've been wasting my time.

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:53.490
No, I don't think that's true.

00:17:55.200 --> 00:17:59.270
I don't completely understand
how the hard suits work.

00:17:59.270 --> 00:18:02.610
Sylia doesn't show me the most important part.

00:18:02.610 --> 00:18:05.240
But it's just a suit.

00:18:05.240 --> 00:18:07.780
If those of us inside the suits don't
work as hard as we can,

00:18:07.780 --> 00:18:09.910
the suit is just a heavy outfit.

00:18:11.550 --> 00:18:13.390
Thank you, Nene.

00:18:13.390 --> 00:18:16.390
If you push yourself like that,
you'll wear yourself out.

00:18:16.390 --> 00:18:17.890
Take it easy.

00:18:17.890 --> 00:18:20.260
Sure. Well, goodnight.

00:18:20.260 --> 00:18:21.320
Goodnight.

00:18:41.850 --> 00:18:43.780
Size 45 wrench.

00:18:45.790 --> 00:18:47.850
Didn't you hear me?

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:49.220
Can I help you now?

00:18:51.190 --> 00:18:52.660
Where is it?

00:18:54.230 --> 00:18:55.690
Yes, Sir!

00:18:59.600 --> 00:19:01.070
Here you go.

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:15.110
Just as I thought, one of the
parts here is missing.

00:19:15.110 --> 00:19:17.080
You go and look for it.

00:19:17.080 --> 00:19:18.550
Where do I look?

00:19:20.820 --> 00:19:24.220
As far as I know, it should
be somewhere upstairs.

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:26.820
I understand. I'll go and look!

00:19:29.030 --> 00:19:32.070
I told him I'd do it, but which
room should I search?

00:19:32.070 --> 00:19:33.760
In this room?

00:19:41.210 --> 00:19:42.280
This room...

00:19:42.280 --> 00:19:44.910
Why is there a boy in here?!

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:46.380
Well...

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:49.710
I'm sorry!

00:19:55.020 --> 00:19:55.990
What's the matter?

00:19:55.990 --> 00:19:56.520
Oh, nothing!
What's the matter?

00:19:56.520 --> 00:19:57.960
Oh, nothing!

00:20:05.160 --> 00:20:06.900
Where the hell did you come from?

00:20:06.900 --> 00:20:09.600
This building is just for girls!

00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:11.940
Well, I'm...

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:14.670
But this man is an exception.

00:20:14.670 --> 00:20:17.300
That's Mackey Stingray.

00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:22.710
Stingray? I didn't know Sylia had a brother.

00:20:24.480 --> 00:20:26.540
How much did you see of me?!

00:20:27.920 --> 00:20:30.120
A little while ago, in the dressing room!

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:31.690
Oh, nothing at all!

00:20:31.690 --> 00:20:34.830
I was hurrying and got out of the room instantly.

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:36.330
I see.

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:39.530
So I didn't see your pink underwear.

00:20:40.900 --> 00:20:42.370
Pink?

00:20:46.240 --> 00:20:47.910
Hey, wait a second!

00:20:47.910 --> 00:20:49.210
I'm so sorry!

00:20:49.210 --> 00:20:50.680
What the hell did you do, kid?!

00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:52.480
I was just talking about the color pink!

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:54.710
Wait just a second!

00:20:55.920 --> 00:20:57.960
Next Episode

00:20:57.960 --> 00:20:58.890
Next Episode
There's a boomer, wandering around town.

00:20:58.890 --> 00:21:00.930
There's a boomer, wandering around town.

00:21:00.930 --> 00:21:04.530
What's his purpose, this boomer
from the bottom of the sea?

00:21:04.530 --> 00:21:08.200
My hard suit is still being repaired!

00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:11.640
I wish I could have sortied
with Priss and Nene.

00:21:11.640 --> 00:21:13.870
What?! Priss's suit hasn't
been fixed yet either?!

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:16.810
What shall we do? We might
be in big trouble!

00:21:16.810 --> 00:21:18.940
Next Bubblegum Crisis!
